(4129380, 589938, 30982, '<td valign="top">What works for this is the bokeh and the single leaf coming up on one side.  What works against it is the light, in a way.  It''s very even but a bit bright, perhaps, which takes away a bit of detail in the petals of the flower - it''s not as rich as it could be, I think.  For flowers to do well in a Free Study, they have to be spectacular.</td>', 'What works for this is the bokeh and the single leaf coming up on one side.  What works against it is the light, in a way.  It''s very even but a bit bright, perhaps, which takes away a bit of detail in the petals of the flower - it''s not as rich as it could be, I think.  For flowers to do well in a Free Study, they have to be spectacular.', '2007-10-01 13:38:31.000000', NULL, 1),
