(4130104, 594082, 73235, '<td valign="top">I have to admit I am not too fond of your picture. There is no detail at all int he sky. The water/waves apear as fog. That''s probably a feature you watned to create. But then the bursts of water spraying up (mid left) don''t fit to this foggy appearance. The beach part on top of the cliffs is washed out, while almost all details in the shadows are gone. May be reducing the shutter speed could give the water back some features. Some minor suggestions: the horizon is tilted, a bit tighter crop at the bottom.<br/>The idea of having the rock in to forground is great, it provides a nice entry into your pic.</td>', 'I have to admit I am not too fond of your picture. There is no detail at all int he sky. The water/waves apear as fog. That''s probably a feature you watned to create. But then the bursts of water spraying up (mid left) don''t fit to this foggy appearance. The beach part on top of the cliffs is washed out, while almost all details in the shadows are gone. May be reducing the shutter speed could give the water back some features. Some minor suggestions: the horizon is tilted, a bit tighter crop at the bottom.The idea of having the rock in to forground is great, it provides a nice entry into your pic.', '2007-10-01 16:26:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(4130111, 594051, 73235, '<td valign="top">nice landscape picture. I love how you anchored the viewer with the post on the left.very inviting to explore more in your picture. congrats a very appealing capture and b/w conversion</td>', 'nice landscape picture. I love how you anchored the viewer with the post on the left.very inviting to explore more in your picture. congrats a very appealing capture and b/w conversion', '2007-10-01 16:29:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(4130141, 594085, 73235, '<td valign="top">It looks like you were fighting a lit with the huge contrast of the sunset, the dark foreground and the dramatic lighting in the clouds. Just an idea: forget the foregrond and crop right where the dark mountains begin and use the coulds as negative space. In advanced editing you could dodge the highlights and burn the dark areas in the clouds much more, making them even more dramatic. You could saturate the cloud colors (mid top) to show the reflections of the sunlight. I love the various layers of mountains in their beautiful shades. I think you wanted to show too much in your picture. May be you could try to go portrait, just showing the mountains and lots of drmatic clouds</td>', 'It looks like you were fighting a lit with the huge contrast of the sunset, the dark foreground and the dramatic lighting in the clouds. Just an idea: forget the foregrond and crop right where the dark mountains begin and use the coulds as negative space. In advanced editing you could dodge the highlights and burn the dark areas in the clouds much more, making them even more dramatic. You could saturate the cloud colors (mid top) to show the reflections of the sunlight. I love the various layers of mountains in their beautiful shades. I think you wanted to show too much in your picture. May be you could try to go portrait, just showing the mountains and lots of drmatic clouds', '2007-10-01 16:37:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(4130146, 593904, 73235, '<td valign="top">nice detailed capture, a bit more sharpness could bring out the eyes more.</td>', 'nice detailed capture, a bit more sharpness could bring out the eyes more.', '2007-10-01 16:37:50.000000', NULL, 1),
