(4133235, 593478, 58728, '<td valign="top">One of my faves so far!  This is awesome.  I love the processing...the colors...and that curtain in the wind is phenomenal.  Very nice lines and composition as well.  10.</td>', 'One of my faves so far!  This is awesome.  I love the processing...the colors...and that curtain in the wind is phenomenal.  Very nice lines and composition as well.  10.', '2007-10-02 13:40:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(4133236, 586453, 73235, '<td valign="top">IMO there are a few thing wrong with this picture. Please do understand my comments as suggestions, not as destructive comments. <br/>Composition: the body positions don''t look very natural. The young woman has to bend her heads so far back that her face is not visible and moves into his shadow. Likewise the young man has to bend forwards casting the shadow onto her face. I can''t help but being distracted by the rose bushes (?) in the background. The choice of background is not very lucky. All these lines cutting into the young couple. Getting the background (may be a brightly lit area as they are wearing dark clothes) away from them separates and solates them from the background. The lower part of your picture is not really adding. Just the opposite. It takes away because its significantly underexposed. You have to look out for details: his right arm is cropped too tight. <br/>Technically the skin is expose well. The hair could use some bounced light. But the biggest point is that the picture is very versy soft. It almost appears as if the wall in the background is more in focus than the couple.<br/>keep participating on this site and check the details of the top 20 picture of each challenge. I know I learned a lot from the great photogs on this site. And I keep learning from my mistakes as this site points them out to you very clearly, sometimes brutally. Keep shooting.</td>', 'IMO there are a few thing wrong with this picture. Please do understand my comments as suggestions, not as destructive comments. Composition: the body positions don''t look very natural. The young woman has to bend her heads so far back that her face is not visible and moves into his shadow. Likewise the young man has to bend forwards casting the shadow onto her face. I can''t help but being distracted by the rose bushes (?) in the background. The choice of background is not very lucky. All these lines cutting into the young couple. Getting the background (may be a brightly lit area as they are wearing dark clothes) away from them separates and solates them from the background. The lower part of your picture is not really adding. Just the opposite. It takes away because its significantly underexposed. You have to look out for details: his right arm is cropped too tight. Technically the skin is expose well. The hair could use some bounced light. But the biggest point is that the picture is very versy soft. It almost appears as if the wall in the background is more in focus than the couple.keep participating on this site and check the details of the top 20 picture of each challenge. I know I learned a lot from the great photogs on this site. And I keep learning from my mistakes as this site points them out to you very clearly, sometimes brutally. Keep shooting.', '2007-10-02 13:40:54.000000', NULL, 1),
