(4145085, 592304, 68586, '<td valign="top">Lovely colours. Good title which could be open to a number of interpretations. Does it mean that the leaves of the clematis are slowly changing from from green to these glorious autumnal shades ? Or is the viewer meant to look at this picture in two sections with the majority of the shot (in autumnal colours) moving in from the left hand side of the shot, and there is now only a tiny sliver of grass left before it catches the green leaves on the right and changes them as well ? (I swear they just got closer while I was typing that) . .<br/> <br/>If you were jsut going for something like the first title then I would have cropped it tighter from the right so that we could just see the great colours - if you were going for something like the second title, then the picture is just perfect. Sadly many won''t get it though. But I like it  :-  )</td>', 'Lovely colours. Good title which could be open to a number of interpretations. Does it mean that the leaves of the clematis are slowly changing from from green to these glorious autumnal shades ? Or is the viewer meant to look at this picture in two sections with the majority of the shot (in autumnal colours) moving in from the left hand side of the shot, and there is now only a tiny sliver of grass left before it catches the green leaves on the right and changes them as well ? (I swear they just got closer while I was typing that) . . If you were jsut going for something like the first title then I would have cropped it tighter from the right so that we could just see the great colours - if you were going for something like the second title, then the picture is just perfect. Sadly many won''t get it though. But I like it  :-  )', '2007-10-05 17:23:00.000000', NULL, 1),
