(4150872, 589684, 61396, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by JaimeVinas:</b></div><hr/><i> I like to know, how did the shadows come up into the sky on this shot? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>These are not shadows, but rather a silhouette of the moving body parts. Using the flash, only the moving parts, captured when the flash was already off, left the apparent "shadows".<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-10-08 02:17:53.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by JaimeVinas: I like to know, how did the shadows come up into the sky on this shot?   These are not shadows, but rather a silhouette of the moving body parts. Using the flash, only the moving parts, captured when the flash was already off, left the apparent "shadows".', '2007-10-08 03:16:50.000000', '2007-10-08 03:17:53.000000', 0),
