(4151025, 585317, 3746, '<td valign="top">Do you always purposely shoot for the brown ribbon? if so then its getting a bit tiresome. On the other hand if you really are trying, then you may need to improve your photographic technique a bit.<br/>for example, you shot this on an OK camera, instead of bumping up the ISO so you can hand hold, stick the camera on a tripod, or rest it on a post/bag etc and use the lowest ISO possible but with a longer shutter speed so the shot doesnt need any `noise removal` afterwards. Also, go easy on the sharpening tools, you have a habit of being a bit too agressive with the sharpness slider.<br/>Then again, if you are intentionally shooting for a low score the carry on as you were..</td>', 'Do you always purposely shoot for the brown ribbon? if so then its getting a bit tiresome. On the other hand if you really are trying, then you may need to improve your photographic technique a bit.for example, you shot this on an OK camera, instead of bumping up the ISO so you can hand hold, stick the camera on a tripod, or rest it on a post/bag etc and use the lowest ISO possible but with a longer shutter speed so the shot doesnt need any `noise removal` afterwards. Also, go easy on the sharpening tools, you have a habit of being a bit too agressive with the sharpness slider.Then again, if you are intentionally shooting for a low score the carry on as you were..', '2007-10-08 05:58:53.000000', NULL, 0),
