(4153428, 593637, 67841, '<td valign="top">Ah, yes - I remember this one during voting.  What a cutie - this really is an absolutely stunning little portrait.  I thought this was an easy top ten candidate but I guess some people just don''t realize how rare these moments are!  I wish I had one nearly as good for one of my daughters...</td>', 'Ah, yes - I remember this one during voting.  What a cutie - this really is an absolutely stunning little portrait.  I thought this was an easy top ten candidate but I guess some people just don''t realize how rare these moments are!  I wish I had one nearly as good for one of my daughters...', '2007-10-09 00:17:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4153458, 593478, 50695, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Rino63:</b></div><hr/><i> I like the right side of this image, the left side with the big white strip is unhelpful in the image. a better composition was possible if the curtain was entire. the crop is distracting and the image lose energy. probably you have only this image, but a second shot with the window on the left and the curtain that fly should be great. the colours and the tones are beautiful. 6 but this is one of that images that I love </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>no no no... why crop out the left side and make a simple image even simpler? and if you include the entire curtain in the frame, then you stabilize it, *reduce* the energy.</td>', 'Originally posted by Rino63: I like the right side of this image, the left side with the big white strip is unhelpful in the image. a better composition was possible if the curtain was entire. the crop is distracting and the image lose energy. probably you have only this image, but a second shot with the window on the left and the curtain that fly should be great. the colours and the tones are beautiful. 6 but this is one of that images that I love   no no no... why crop out the left side and make a simple image even simpler? and if you include the entire curtain in the frame, then you stabilize it, *reduce* the energy.', '2007-10-09 00:25:45.000000', NULL, 0),
