(4174209, 592990, 68035, '<td valign="top">Gee Roz, sorry it has taken me so long to comment on this magnificent shot<br/> <br/>Huge congratulations on the 7ths place (in a free study!!!!!!!!) the new personal best and on breaking the 7 barrier for the first time<br/> <br/>A brilliant image that almost blurs the line between photography, painting and CGI such is its power and intensity<br/> <br/>The subject matter is magnificently disturbing, it looks like a scene from hell and the orange hue that you have included just intensifies the feeling of heat fire and almost a choking atmosphere<br/> <br/>Brilliant!!!!!!!</td>', 'Gee Roz, sorry it has taken me so long to comment on this magnificent shot Huge congratulations on the 7ths place (in a free study!!!!!!!!) the new personal best and on breaking the 7 barrier for the first time A brilliant image that almost blurs the line between photography, painting and CGI such is its power and intensity The subject matter is magnificently disturbing, it looks like a scene from hell and the orange hue that you have included just intensifies the feeling of heat fire and almost a choking atmosphere Brilliant!!!!!!!', '2007-10-17 06:46:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4174252, 593137, 68035, '<td valign="top">Ha...who needs a high score when you get to photograph something as cool as this.  I still cant get over that little critters splayed feet and I love the background of pond weed.  A shot that will always make me smile</td>', 'Ha...who needs a high score when you get to photograph something as cool as this.  I still cant get over that little critters splayed feet and I love the background of pond weed.  A shot that will always make me smile', '2007-10-17 06:56:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4174264, 586664, 68035, '<td valign="top">Sandy, I was shocked that this did not finish higher in the FS as I thought it was a nailed on ribbon when I saw it<br/> <br/>I love the fact that you have got a great deal of softness in the image and that the colours almost look pastel.  This contrasts wonderfully with the pure strength of the stag (though its expression is one of tender/kindness rather than any type of threat or aggression)<br/> <br/>Super composition as well, another simply breathtaking image</td>', 'Sandy, I was shocked that this did not finish higher in the FS as I thought it was a nailed on ribbon when I saw it I love the fact that you have got a great deal of softness in the image and that the colours almost look pastel.  This contrasts wonderfully with the pure strength of the stag (though its expression is one of tender/kindness rather than any type of threat or aggression) Super composition as well, another simply breathtaking image', '2007-10-17 07:03:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4174398, 591962, 54033, '<td valign="top">You have to be a pilot to appreciate such a great shot!! I will do a flight plan now from Amman-Marka (AMM/OJAM) to Sharm El-Shiekh International Airport - Ophira (SSH/HESH) and take of. I can not stand bearing the feel of the need to fly.<br/><b>I have control.</b> <br/>Your photo will cost me at least $1500<br/></td>', 'You have to be a pilot to appreciate such a great shot!! I will do a flight plan now from Amman-Marka (AMM/OJAM) to Sharm El-Shiekh International Airport - Ophira (SSH/HESH) and take of. I can not stand bearing the feel of the need to fly.I have control. Your photo will cost me at least $1500', '2007-10-17 08:33:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4174436, 592074, 30982, '<td valign="top">I, for one, really like your style.  It may not score well, but it''s very good.  This is an excellent example - this is a fine "in the moment" capture with a great deal of life to it.  It''s well composed, well exposed, and has just the right touch of post processing - at least in my uneducated opinion.  Yet for DPC, it''s not "flashy" enough - and I certainly wouldn''t want it any flashier.  It has DPC-technical-flaws - blown highlights, cutoff head, cutoff arms - all of which, in my opinion, serve the composition well.  So do what you do - there are some of us out here who really appreciate it.  And I''m betting your friend liked this, too - did he put it up on his myspace page?</td>', 'I, for one, really like your style.  It may not score well, but it''s very good.  This is an excellent example - this is a fine "in the moment" capture with a great deal of life to it.  It''s well composed, well exposed, and has just the right touch of post processing - at least in my uneducated opinion.  Yet for DPC, it''s not "flashy" enough - and I certainly wouldn''t want it any flashier.  It has DPC-technical-flaws - blown highlights, cutoff head, cutoff arms - all of which, in my opinion, serve the composition well.  So do what you do - there are some of us out here who really appreciate it.  And I''m betting your friend liked this, too - did he put it up on his myspace page?', '2007-10-17 08:50:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4174612, 590340, 74979, '<td valign="top">what a great POV!  lovely image</td>', 'what a great POV!  lovely image', '2007-10-17 10:02:29.000000', NULL, 0),
