(4265589, 593379, 69368, '<td valign="top">I''m sure, it was hard for you... first entry and your first  free study...<br/>It''s a nice pic, interesting play with lighting and colors. But if you like to get a better score, is this not a good idea for free study. It''s not enough DPC-friendly, IMO<br/> <br/>don''t worry! Good luck for your next entry!</td>', 'I''m sure, it was hard for you... first entry and your first  free study...It''s a nice pic, interesting play with lighting and colors. But if you like to get a better score, is this not a good idea for free study. It''s not enough DPC-friendly, IMO don''t worry! Good luck for your next entry!', '2007-11-23 09:52:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(4270020, 593478, 63269, '<td valign="top">I really, <i>really</i> like the extreme vibrance of the orange... usually when you pull the saturation up this much, it looks awful. But there is just the perfect amount of variation in the hue of the color, and just enough texture to make this interesting, instead of painful to look at. Then something about the high-contrast, the dash of blue, and the pure white of the curtain.... this is a really fun, powerful image!</td>', 'I really, really like the extreme vibrance of the orange... usually when you pull the saturation up this much, it looks awful. But there is just the perfect amount of variation in the hue of the color, and just enough texture to make this interesting, instead of painful to look at. Then something about the high-contrast, the dash of blue, and the pure white of the curtain.... this is a really fun, powerful image!', '2007-11-26 16:33:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4276107, 593733, 87167, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by yanko:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by JohnnyPhD:</b></div><hr/><i> The glow is uneven around the person, which takes away from the purpose of the shot (atleast according to the title) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I was trying to say the same thing but my comment didn''t register since the challenge ended. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Interesting, except for the fact that the glow does go all around her, albeit heavier in some areas than other, but I don''t see how that is an issue, it doesn''t change the fact that there is a glow or halo around the model, I don''t think it was ever implied that it was an "even" glow.  I think it works perfectly for the photographer''s vision and purpose of the shot.</td>', 'Originally posted by yanko: Originally posted by JohnnyPhD: The glow is uneven around the person, which takes away from the purpose of the shot (atleast according to the title)   I was trying to say the same thing but my comment didn''t register since the challenge ended.   Interesting, except for the fact that the glow does go all around her, albeit heavier in some areas than other, but I don''t see how that is an issue, it doesn''t change the fact that there is a glow or halo around the model, I don''t think it was ever implied that it was an "even" glow.  I think it works perfectly for the photographer''s vision and purpose of the shot.', '2007-11-29 12:09:43.000000', NULL, 0),
