(4329404, 593425, 60862, '<td valign="top">How''s the layer practice coming?  Aside from using a soft light layer (<a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=55" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">see idnic''s excellent tutorial</a>), try using a reflector to bounce light back onto her face from below.  I use a piece of white posterboard - it doesn''t have to be expensive.  Her eyes are so beautiful, you want them to shine. :)</td>', 'How''s the layer practice coming?  Aside from using a soft light layer (see idnic''s excellent tutorial), try using a reflector to bounce light back onto her face from below.  I use a piece of white posterboard - it doesn''t have to be expensive.  Her eyes are so beautiful, you want them to shine. :)', '2007-12-22 01:33:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(4329432, 593425, 19708, '<td valign="top">I''ll add to this.<br/>In Photoshop, take this image as it is here, and try this:<br/>Image, Adjustments, Match Color, then in the settings box, check Neutralize, then slide the Luminescence slider on the top to about 130.<br/>A one-step quick color correction while maintaining the soft pastel feel here.</td>', 'I''ll add to this.In Photoshop, take this image as it is here, and try this:Image, Adjustments, Match Color, then in the settings box, check Neutralize, then slide the Luminescence slider on the top to about 130.A one-step quick color correction while maintaining the soft pastel feel here.', '2007-12-22 02:27:45.000000', NULL, 0),
